# Intent Chips Only Move Forward

A transcript is a path, not a menu. Once the member has moved past a row of
intent chips, that row is **history**: every chip in it goes disabled and
takes no click. Only the newest row — the one that carries the conversation
forward — is live. This is app-wide and permanent.

## What this means on the surface

- Tap a chip → the turn plays, and the row you tapped is now dimmed and inert.
- Scroll back three turns → those chips read as disabled. Hovering does
  nothing, tapping does nothing, Tab skips them.
- The row trailing the newest answer is the only one you can act on.
- One step can own several rows. The signup multi-select posts its
  suggestions and its Continue / Skip controls as two rows, and the portfolio
  posts its report scopes as three — a run of **adjacent sibling** rows is one
  step and stays live together.

## What is never locked

- **Output chips**, preview cards, version thumbnails, citation markers, and
  anything else that opens a module. An output the member never opened must
  still open three turns later — see the outputs-open-on-request rule.
- **`.sc-inline-chips`**, the shared row the chat re-parks at the end of the
  thread after every reply. It is a single element that moves, so it is the
  live row by construction.
- Welcome chips and the persistent rail. They are not in the transcript.

## How it is wired

Shared module: `js/chip-lock.js`, injected from `js/agent-menu.js` on every
page that renders the WISE nav, and loaded directly by `create-account.html`
(no nav). It watches every transcript (`.chat-messages-area` / `#chat-messages`)
and stamps `data-chips-spent` on each spent row; `pages/wise.css` gives that
attribute the disabled look in both themes. Locking is sticky — transcripts
only grow, and a thread saved to history restores in the state it was saved in.

A row is spent when the member has said something beneath it (a `.sc-line-you`
landed below) or a newer chip row has arrived beneath it.

## Rules for the agent

- Never re-enable a past chip row, and never add a "replay this step" path.
- Do not fork this per page. A host that knows it has just left every open
  step calls `WiseChipLock.lockPrior(messagesEl)`; everything else is handled
  by the observer — see the nothing-page-local rule.
- A new chip-row class must be added to `ROW_SEL` in `js/chip-lock.js`, not
  handled with a page-local disabler.
- If a new control genuinely must stay tappable forever, add it to `KEEP_SEL`
  — do not opt the whole row out.
